{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116130",
      "title": "Change Detection During Development: ExpressionChangedAfterChecked Errors",
      "lectureOrder": 196,
      "videoOrder": 188,
      "sourceHash": "41ea499c679a70612a00104f0ea3b68ede56cc8400d87193161a7616c3cb84ca",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "So, why do we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 5.67,
          "en": "this duplicate log output here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.67,
          "end": 9.3,
          "en": "Why are all these components visited twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 10.92,
          "en": "after our changes?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 13.203,
          "en": "So when I changed the counter, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.4,
          "end": 17.16,
          "en": "Well, that only happens during development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.16,
          "end": 19.53,
          "en": "If you were to build this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.53,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "for production and deploy it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 24.84,
          "en": "you would not have this behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.84,
          "end": 26.34,
          "en": "Instead, this is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.34,
          "end": 30.33,
          "en": "a development mode feature provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.33,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "because in development mode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "it runs change detection twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 38.55,
          "en": "to detect unwanted value changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 42.45,
          "en": "that might happen after change detection was executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.45,
          "end": 45.54,
          "en": "That's why it executes it twice to see if",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 49.383,
          "en": "the value produced by the first cycle then suddenly changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "And an example for such an unwanted change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 57.66,
          "en": "would be, for example, in the InfoMessage Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.66,
          "end": 62.133,
          "en": "if in the debugOutput you would return a random value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.81,
          "end": 66.45,
          "en": "This value, since it's random,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.45,
          "end": 69.69,
          "en": "is not stable and will not be the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.69,
          "end": 72.9,
          "en": "between two change detection cycles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.9,
          "end": 76.28999999999999,
          "en": "Instead, a new random value will be generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.28999999999999,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "on average change detection run,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 80.85,
          "en": "and therefore if Angular performs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.85,
          "end": 84.36,
          "en": "two change detection cycles directly after each other,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.36,
          "end": 87.93,
          "en": "it'll be two different values that will be detected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.93,
          "end": 91.35,
          "en": "and that will cause an error, as you see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.35,
          "end": 92.91,
          "en": "If you reload, you get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.91,
          "end": 95.94,
          "en": "and if you now change the counter, you also get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.94,
          "end": 97.85300000000001,
          "en": "You get an ExpressionChangedAfterItHasBeenCheckedError,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 104.22,
          "en": "which is Angular's way of telling you that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.22,
          "end": 105.84,
          "en": "the value that was found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.84,
          "end": 108.9,
          "en": "during the second development mode only",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.9,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "changed detection cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 112.22999999999999,
          "en": "is different from the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.22999999999999,
          "end": 114.453,
          "en": "that was found in the first cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.28999999999999,
          "end": 118.35300000000001,
          "en": "It actually even tells you that here in the error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.25,
          "end": 121.53,
          "en": "And therefore, if you happen to encounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.53,
          "end": 125.22,
          "en": "an error like this in your Angular application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.22,
          "end": 128.7,
          "en": "it is likely that somewhere in the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.7,
          "end": 131.4,
          "en": "probably in the place that's highlighted here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.4,
          "end": 134.61,
          "en": "you have code that changes data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 138.18,
          "en": "that's being shown on the screen in an unintended way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.18,
          "end": 140.763,
          "en": "and that you have a potential bug in your code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 144.93,
          "en": "That's why here, I'll go back to that fixed string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.93,
          "end": 149.57999999999998,
          "en": "which of course is stable and won't change between cycles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.57999999999998,
          "end": 151.8,
          "en": "So that's where this error is coming from,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.8,
          "end": 153.51,
          "en": "and why during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.51,
          "end": 156.78,
          "en": "Angular runs change detection twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.78,
          "end": 161.22,
          "en": "But now let's take a look at how we can potentially optimize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.22,
          "end": 163.44299999999998,
          "en": "Angular's change detection behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
